  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Two key sounds",
   "texto": [
    "The **sch** group always sounds like a soft and continuous «sh»: **Tschüss** (goodbye), **Schmidt**, **schreibt** (writing), **Entschuldigung** (forgiveness).",
    "The **ch** combination has two pronouncements according to the previous vocal:",
    "1. **Ich-Laut** (soft): after **e, i** or consonant, it sounds like a very soft jota and advanced to the palate: **ich** (I), **mich** (to me), **nicht** (no).",
    "2. **Ach-Laut** (strong): after **a, o, u**, it sounds further back in the throat, similar to the Spanish jota: **auch** (also), **noch** (still), **Nachname** (last name)."
   ]
  },
